    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=MKG535": {
      "title": "Applicant Services Assistant x2",
      "description": "MKG535 Applicant Services Assistant x2 - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Applicant Services Assistant x2 Job Details: Job Description Middlesex University, London The role: Join our Applicant Services team and play a key part in shaping the future of our student community. As an Applicant Services Assistant, you will be at the heart of our recruitment process, ensuring a smooth, efficient, and fair journey for every applicant. You will take responsibility for assessing applications with accuracy and care, while also providing clear and helpful guidance to prospective students. Your work will directly support the University’s recruitment goals and deliver an excellent first impression of Middlesex. Key Responsibilities: •Undertake the fair and efficient assessment of applications against set entry criteria. •Provide accurate and timely guidance to prospective students on their application status and next steps. •Ensure the integrity and smooth progression of the admissions process. •Maintain precise and up-to-date applicant records. •Contribute to a high-quality applicant experience that reflects our university values. About you: You are highly organised, possess excellent attention to detail, and can work effectively to deadlines. With strong written and verbal communication skills, you can explain information clearly and provide excellent customer service. A collaborative team member, with a proactive approach, you are keen to contribute to a vital university function. Experience in an administrative, customer service, or education setting is desirable. For further information, please contact Gifty Ohemeng, Applicant Services Manager: g.ohemeng@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Global Marketing & Recruitment Company MU Services Ltd Location Hendon Starting Salary £28,840\r\n            per annum Grade Grade 4 Contract Type Permanent Hours per Week 35.5 Date Posted Thursday 15 October 2026 Closing Date Friday 30 October 2026 Reference MKG535 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
