    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=MKG534": {
      "title": "MKG534 Student Visa Compliance Officer",
      "description": "MKG534 Student Visa Compliance Officer - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register More ▼ Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ More ▼ Student Visa Compliance Officer Job Details: Job Description We are looking for a dedicated Visa Compliance Officer to ensure the University meets its critical United Kingdom Visa & Immigration (UKVI) sponsorship duties. You will play a lead role in maintaining our sponsor licence and visa compliance amongst our international student visa-holder community You will coordinate key compliance activities, from admissions checks and new student registration to the ongoing monitoring of existing students. A central responsibility will be managing our student attendance and engagement monitoring processes and associated reporting obligations. We are seeking an experienced compliance professional with in-depth knowledge of UKVI Student Route regulations. You are meticulous, proactive, and possess strong leadership skills to develop robust processes and guide university staff. Experience in a Higher Education setting or relevant regulatory/compliance environment is essential. For enquiries about the post, please contact Manesh Hanj, Student Visa Compliance Manager: m.hanj@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic groups, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Global Marketing & Recruitment Company MU Services Ltd Location Hendon Starting Salary £37,357\n            per annum Grade Grade 6 Contract Type Fixed Term - 12 months Hours per Week 35.5 Date Posted Wednesday 14 October 2026 Closing Date Friday 30 October 2026 Reference MKG534 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
