    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=ACI211": {
      "title": "Graduate Academic Assistant (Fashion Communication)",
      "description": "ACI211 Graduate Academic Assistant (Fashion Communication) - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Graduate Academic Assistant (Fashion Communication) Job Details: Job Description Middlesex University is looking for a Graduate Academic Assistant in the Directorate of Creative Practices, for the Fashion Programmes. Middlesex University brings together over 35,000 students across campuses in London, Dubai and Mauritius, academics at the top of their game, and an international network of industry partners in our global community to learn, discover and innovate. The Directorate of Creative Practices comprises of Fashion Communication and Styling, Fashion Marketing, Fashion Design and Fine Art. The well-resourced Grove buildings in our north London campus have modern arts facilities housing a diverse international community of staff and students. Graduate Academic Assistants (GAAs) have an invaluable role at Middlesex, assisting and supporting academics in the facilitation of learning and teaching, dissemination of research and knowledge exchange, and enhancing student experience and employability. You will join an established team of GAAs and work with experienced academics across all the subjects in the Directorate. This role is best suited to a recent graduate or postgraduate with a degree in a relevant Fashion subject, aiming at an academic or professional career within the HE and/or arts and creative sector. For informal enquiries, please contact Lucy Fine, Director of Creative Practices Programmes, via email at L.Fine@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment where everyone can thrive. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups, including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit.\r\n\r\nWe value the diverse perspectives, experiences and talents that people from all backgrounds bring to our global community. Please note that applicants must already have the right to work in the UK, as visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Faculty of Arts & Creative Industries Company Middlesex University Location Hendon Starting Salary £29,417\r\n            per annum Grade Grade 4 Contract Type Fixed Term - 7 months Hours per Week 35.5 Date Posted Monday 26 October 2026 Closing Date Wednesday 11 November 2026 Reference ACI211 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
    },
    "https://jobs.mdx.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=FIN570": {
      "title": "FIN570 Senior Research Finance Administrator",
      "description": "FIN570 Senior Research Finance Administrator - Careers at Middlesex University Skip to main content Home Login Register Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Home Login Register More ▼ Home Login Register Careers at MDX Careers at Middlesex Jobs Home Current Vacancies How to Apply Contact Us FAQ More ▼ Senior Research Finance Administrator Job Details: Job Description Join Our Finance Team at Middlesex University. Middlesex University is seeking a dedicated Senior Research Finance Administrator to join our Financial Services team during an exciting period of transformation. This role will act as a specialist practitioner in research finance, applying professional knowledge of post-award financial management, funder regulations, and University policies to ensure compliant and effective administration of a significant portfolio of research awards. You will work closely with a variety of stakeholders across the University from Financial Services, Academic Services to Professional Services, to provide oversight of the financial administration of a wide portfolio of research-related grants. Your work will directly support our mission to deliver an outstanding educational experience while maintaining robust financial governance. Middlesex University is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. We warmly welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds and value the diverse perspectives and talents they bring to our global community. For further information about the role, please contact Vicnan Anandakumar, Finance Business Partner, via email at v.anandakumar@mdx.ac.uk Middlesex is committed to fostering an inclusive working environment where everyone can thrive. We encourage applications from underrepresented groups, including people from Black, Asian and minority ethnic backgrounds, disabled people, LGBTQ+ people, women, and gender non-conforming individuals. All recruitment decisions will be based on merit.\n\nWe value the diverse perspectives, experiences and talents that people from all backgrounds bring to our global community. Please note that applicants must already have the right to work in the UK, as visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Email details to a friend Apply Online We value diversity and strive to create a fairer, more equitable work environment for our staff and students. We offer a range of family friendly, inclusive employment policies, flexible working arrangements, staff diversity networks, campus facilities and services to support staff from different backgrounds. Middlesex is home to a diverse community of professionals. We are a bronze award holder of the Athena Swan Charter and the Race Equality Charter, a Stonewall Top 100 employer and Gold award holder in 2023, and a Disability Confident Leader. Share: View All Vacancies Job Details Faculty/Executive Finance Company MU Services Ltd Location Hendon Starting Salary £37,357\n            per annum Grade Grade 6 Contract Type Permanent Hours per Week 35.5 Date Posted Friday 23 October 2026 Closing Date Sunday 15 November 2026 Reference FIN570 Apply Online Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs Search Advanced Job Search Useful Links Careers at Middlesex About Us MU Services Limited Existing Account / Staff Member Do you have an existing account, or are you a member of staff? Login New User For new applicants, please register for an account Register Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility"
